from a show about humans versus titans  to a show about  war racism injustice and freedom attack  on titan has come a long way now hasn't  it with season four coming to a rather  cliffhanging conclusion we can call it  the season that revolutionized anime  and gave us one of the greatest main  characters of all time so as a tribute  to the series i'm going to take a look  at 10 of the best moments in the fourth  season of attack on titan  also a quick reminder to subscribe to  our channel if you haven't because we've  got a lot more content like this coming  your way with that said let's dive into  the list  talk about bad karma you enter and  massacre an entire city of malians  and they come back to massacre yours you  eat one of their titans in the most  brutal way possible  well they just eat your legs this scene  not only showed marley's skill and  espionage but showed peak's potential to  be a great actress her convincing powers  were insane  and even managed to give gabby some  lessons on morality also let's not  forget that shot of the attack titan now  looking like the true devil of parodies  overall this can be called one of the  greatest cliffhanger season endings of  all time  and eren's battle call for rhino was  both chilling and suspenseful  we may have to wait yet another year but  i'm looking forward to the confrontation  between the two parties  three titans versus one the  possibilities are endless  and that's why this scene is such a  strong cliffhanger  [Music]  when a character can turn into a large  ape who's a pro baseball player  and a mass murderer you gotta wonder  about his origin story  zeke at first wasn't a face to anyone  like to see the hatred of killing  humanity's greatest commander still lay  in our minds and even though levi gave  him the punishment he deserved  zeke still ranked top in isaiah's i'm  never gonna kill them list  fortunately to justify his experience of  plot armor we got a flashback of his  past which once again proved that no  person in the attack on titan universe  has ever had a happy beginning  grisha back in the day was a much more  motivated and a psychologically abusive  fire that no kid would like to have  that's when we realized that only a  fragment of what happened back in season  three was revealed  zeke tried to convince his parents to  give up for their own safety but when  they didn't he had to spill out  everything for the man he knew  this not only made zeke yeager a tragic  anti-hero but also a character we can  sympathize with  [Music]  [Music]  coming in at number eight is erin's  conversation with mikasa and armin  so moving back to erin not only does he  decide to do a prison break but to also  casually walk in and have a chat with  his old friends okay perhaps  chatting is the wrong word but how about  emotionally traumatizing one character  and physically abusing the other yep  this scene may just pass on as another  scene filled with overbombastic dialogue  but don't forget the words  and punches that were exchanged in the  process aaron entered the room as armin  and mikasa's childhood friend but walked  away after shattering his relationship  with both of them and we finally got to  know why mikasa was such a flat  character through the first two seasons  so props to isaiah for finally  correcting his own writing mistakes  next up we have levi and the survey  corps entrance in mali  normally when you see your favorite  characters after a time skip that puts a  smile on your face but in attack on  titan  it does the exact opposite i know we had  quite a few hype moments with the acumen  entrances and the appearance of jean and  the rest of the gang but let's not also  forget the casualties both sides  suffered and if you're a manga reader  you might note that little detail studio  mapper added to make the morality of  each character more ambiguous who are  the good guys who are the bad guys the  eldians and their titans are trying to  defend their nation and the soldiers of  parodies are taking their revenge no  one's right or wrong  and at the end of the day you can't  really pick sides okay well perhaps we  all hate gabby but at least admit you  rooted for the rest of the characters  [Music]  next let's move on to another tragic  backstory that's bertolt reiner and  annie's mission on parodies  honestly this season of attack on titan  is like one of those truth-revealing  arcs in higurashi  every mystery plot thread and character  arc the previous seasons built up was  either resolved or justified the same  can be said for our original malian trio  reiner's words at the top of the wall  before the reveal annie's desire to see  her father all of these were given a  purpose through the backstory we also  got more character insight into rhino as  we realized how tragic his own past is  and how he finally built up the courage  to lead the team after getting kicked by  annie and like most flashbacks in attack  on titan  in the end every character had a reason  for doing what they did there were no  villains in attack on titan  just flawed people  [Music]  foreign  those who started sympathizing with zeke  we deeply regret to inform you that next  up is the third round of levi  and zeke by now even without watching  the scene you should know how this works  levi ackermann's another arnold's  voldigold but with blades you can't kill  him you can't hurt him and even if you  turn all his comrades into titans he  still catches up to you because this man  has no regrets  at first zeke and levi seem like the  perfect duo like two rivals who can't  help but work together then  zeke turns the tables transforms levi's  whole squad into titans and executes the  perfect backstab of all time  at this point levi has faced enough  tragedy that he's grown numb to him he  reminisces with his squad for one last  time  and the slashing begins zeke's cgi titan  couldn't once again take down the  ackerman and though it wasn't some  brutal slugfest like last time levi won  the round easily and taught the elder  jaeger brother the consequences of  messing with an ackermann  coming in at number four is the opening  sequence of season four  war can be brutal and that's something  you've heard more than a million times  have you ever seen a war with explosive  trains and overpowered titans once again  studio mapper  just built the infrastructure of the  scene using the manga and added their  own formula to make this scene extra  brutal dead bodies  explosions blood splatters brutal deaths  all of them amalgamated to give us a  well-directed scene that showed how  horrible the war is and also let's not  forget about ryan and zeke who stole the  spotlight of the scene with their  transformations  gabby's energetic character introduction  and marley's brutal war tactics the very  first attack on titan scene directed by  mapa ended with flying colours and at  the same time  we had to stare in awe at the power of  mali surely aaron is no match for this  well at least that's what we thought  next up at number three is erin's fight  with the warhammer titan  what's the most creative way to slay a  titan ask aaron yeager he may have been  the crying and screaming protagonist in  season one but now he's back with more  muscle  more brain power and little to no  morality in this fight evan uses a lot  of strategies compared to his previous  fights with titans and was even quick to  figure out the trick of the warhammer  titan he did get some help from mikasa  and his squad mates but he did most of  the job and the eating the sequence of  him devouring lara taibo with jaw titan  as the nutcracker was one of the most  brutal scenes in attack on titan and all  that time i had my mouth open wondering  how much aaron had changed remember when  i said eren's no match for mali after  this scene  it was the other way around  [Music]  coming in at number two is armin's  transformation in liberio all this  season we've been talking about aaron  and marley so let's shine the spotlight  on our blonde strategist shall we after  getting burnt to death armin seems to  like burning other people to death  that's exactly what happened during his  transformation in liberio however unlike  erin armin seems to regret what happened  and seems depressed about the events  looking at it from a certain perspective  you have to sympathize with him he  sacrificed himself for the colossal  titan with a firm resolve but then he  was resurrected  forced to wield the power of the  colossal titan and then thrown into a  racist war  where he had to kill people like i said  you find tragedy all around season four  but if you divert away from that  pessimistic viewpoint you can also call  this scene one of the best anime  transformations of all time  oh taking our first spot is the  ever-famous errands transformation in  liberio how long has it been  three years well if you weren't a manga  reader you never know how much hype we  were for this scene if you're an anime  only viewer then i can tell you without  a doubt your jaw fell onto the floor  during the grand reveal this scene isn't  just one of the greatest scenes of  attack on titan but the scene that  changed the main character  showed who held the upper hand and  showed the potential of the show as a  whole the tension was neatly built up  during the conversation of erin and  reiner and then with one flash of  lightning the narrative of attack on  titan flipped of 180 and turned to be  one of the greatest stories ever written  surely this is a scene that will be  talked about for ages on social media  so there goes our picks for 10 of the  best attack on titan season 4 moments  all our prayers are for studio maplight  to adapt the rest of the series and  bring it to a successful conclusion and  judging from the popularity of the  series  i can definitely tell our prayers will  be answered let me know your favorite  moments down below in the comments and  make sure to like the video if you  enjoyed it that's it for today anime  fans and i'll see you in the next video  you

